The Galil DMC-41x3 driver now retries empty or malformed controller replies when polling motion status and axis positions, and waiting for motion to complete is bounded by a timeout (300 s by default) that raises ``TimeoutError``. Each motion-status query is limited by the remaining motion timeout, with millisecond resolution, and restores the original I/O timeout afterward. Connecting now falls back through the ``--direct -s ALL`` and ``-s ALL`` options before using the bare address. Pressing Ctrl-C while waiting for motion now calls ``abort()`` and then turns the axes off with ``MO``.
